# Infrastructure Standards

Infrastructure work must comply with:

- `specs/README.md`
- `specs/security/SEC-001-security-baseline.md`
- `specs/security/SEC-002-security-testing.md`

SEC-001 defines required protections. SEC-002 defines the evidence required to validate them.

Mandatory infrastructure expectations:

- public exposure limited to intended HTTP/HTTPS entrypoints;
- DB, Redis, internal services, metrics and admin docs must not be publicly exposed;
- use HTTPS, HSTS, secure headers and managed certificate renewal in production;
- run containers as non-root where possible and avoid privileged mounts such as docker.sock;
- scan dependencies, containers and secrets in CI/CD;
- block production release on critical security findings or failed security gates.
